# Lingerlong: a marble plaza in the sky where it is always the same late afternoon, the place everyone
# meets. Less a tune than a warm hum to sit in: a hazy pad that wavers like warm air over marble, an old
# electric piano heard from across the square turning slowly through each chord, a soft round bass, and
# a few high notes now and then like the sun catching the fountain. Major sevenths throughout, lots of
# room, no drums. D major, 60 bpm. Instruments of its own: haze and epiano.

title Lingerlong
tempo 60
beats 4
steps 2
seed  171

voice hum    kind=haze    octave=4  gain=0.50  reverb=0.6
voice bass   kind=bass    octave=2  gain=0.22  reverb=0.3
voice keys   kind=epiano  octave=4  gain=0.34  pan=-0.2  reverb=0.55
voice bell   kind=epiano  octave=5  gain=0.20  pan=0.25  reverb=0.7
voice sun    kind=chime   octave=6  gain=0.16  spread=0.6 reverb=0.85

[a]
chords | Dmaj7 | Bm9 | Gmaj7 | Em9 | Dmaj7 | F#m7 | Gmaj7 | Asus4 |
hum    | * - - - - - - - |
bass   | 1 - - - - - - - |
keys   | 1 . . 3 . . 2 . |
